WEBVTT

00:00:18.330 --> 00:00:19.210
Idiot...

00:01:56.800 --> 00:01:57.940
You're so weird!

00:01:57.940 --> 00:02:01.920
~ Such an airhead with that goofy hairdo. ~

00:02:01.920 --> 00:02:04.060
Jeez... Cut it out!

00:02:05.750 --> 00:02:07.890
He's going to score if this keeps up.

00:02:07.890 --> 00:02:09.770
Someone stop 'im!

00:02:11.840 --> 00:02:14.360
We're exhausted just from chasing them.

00:02:14.360 --> 00:02:16.990
Over here! Over here!

00:02:16.990 --> 00:02:19.200
Got it! Got it! Got it!

00:02:20.520 --> 00:02:21.460
Coming through!

00:02:21.460 --> 00:02:22.860
Over there, I'll pass it to you.

00:02:22.860 --> 00:02:23.850
Okay.

00:02:32.090 --> 00:02:35.240
Wow! She's so cool!

00:02:35.240 --> 00:02:37.080
It's so nice being tall.

00:02:37.080 --> 00:02:39.010
I envy her.

00:02:46.680 --> 00:02:48.140
Laugh and Forgive Me!?

00:02:52.480 --> 00:02:54.230
Darn it all.

00:02:54.230 --> 00:02:59.830
We might have won if you didn't let Okuyama steal the ball.

00:02:59.830 --> 00:03:01.300
Shut up!

00:03:01.300 --> 00:03:02.660
Hey, ya doin' yer job?

00:03:02.660 --> 00:03:04.870
What? Don't just watch. Help us out!

00:03:06.060 --> 00:03:10.370
You were the ones who suggested that the losers clean up.

00:03:10.370 --> 00:03:12.830
Hmph! You only won because of Okuyama.

00:03:12.830 --> 00:03:14.220
Oh well.

00:03:14.220 --> 00:03:17.300
Just leave all height-related sports to me.

00:03:17.300 --> 00:03:19.890
Why don't we make Okuyama clean up?

00:03:19.890 --> 00:03:21.040
What!?

00:03:21.040 --> 00:03:22.220
And why do you say that?

00:03:22.220 --> 00:03:25.230
I agree. Okuyama is like an Amazon girl.

00:03:25.230 --> 00:03:27.640
I'm sure you can clean it up by yourself.

00:03:28.600 --> 00:03:34.060
Yeah! Yeah! You Amazon girl! You gorilla girl!

00:03:34.060 --> 00:03:36.690
Hey! Don't say things like that!
Gorilla girl!

00:03:43.260 --> 00:03:44.490
Awesome!

00:03:44.490 --> 00:03:46.050
Okuyama-san, you're great!

00:03:46.050 --> 00:03:47.450
Get 'em! Get 'em!

00:03:48.050 --> 00:03:49.180
Darn it!

00:03:49.180 --> 00:03:50.690
I can't breath!

00:03:50.690 --> 00:03:52.350
Stop it!

00:03:52.350 --> 00:03:53.660
I-I give up!

00:03:53.660 --> 00:03:56.760
No, I'll never give up!

00:03:56.760 --> 00:03:59.160
Stop struggling.

00:03:59.160 --> 00:04:00.900
I can't breath either.

00:04:00.900 --> 00:04:02.630
Well? Do you surrender?

00:04:02.630 --> 00:04:04.030
Yes, I do.

00:04:04.030 --> 00:04:04.980
Surrender.

00:04:05.930 --> 00:04:09.700
Next time, don't say something like that to Okuyama-san again.

00:04:09.700 --> 00:04:10.600
Yeah, yeah.

00:04:11.310 --> 00:04:13.210
I haven't given up yet.

00:04:13.210 --> 00:04:14.310
Not yet?

00:04:16.360 --> 00:04:18.350
I'll never do it again.

00:04:18.350 --> 00:04:20.740
Leave us alone, just clean up!

00:04:22.030 --> 00:04:24.290
It's not funny anymore!

00:04:24.290 --> 00:04:25.890
Anyway... Run!

00:04:25.890 --> 00:04:27.240
Come back here!

00:04:27.240 --> 00:04:28.620
Let's split up!

00:04:28.620 --> 00:04:29.740
Alright!

00:04:31.310 --> 00:04:34.670
Why are you chasing only me? Get away from me!

00:04:34.670 --> 00:04:36.130
I won't forgive you!

00:04:38.150 --> 00:04:39.840
Stop, Sagawa!

00:04:39.840 --> 00:04:43.470
They're always the ones left fighting every time.

00:04:43.470 --> 00:04:45.570
Maybe they're born rivals.

00:04:45.570 --> 00:04:47.440
There ain't nothin' we can do about those two.

00:04:47.440 --> 00:04:50.140
But they always look like they're having fun.

00:04:50.140 --> 00:04:53.820
Okuyama-san is so strong.

00:04:53.820 --> 00:04:55.820
She's like my idol!

00:04:55.820 --> 00:04:58.520
Hadzuki-chan, she ain't an actress, y'know.

00:05:00.440 --> 00:05:05.700
Wow, Okuyama-san is so wonderful. She's like those actresses that play male roles.

00:05:05.700 --> 00:05:07.630
Not at all.

00:05:07.630 --> 00:05:11.520
I'm just good at height-related sports.

00:05:11.520 --> 00:05:13.370
I'm not good at anything else.

00:05:13.370 --> 00:05:17.880
That's not true! Height is important in everything!

00:05:17.880 --> 00:05:19.430
You think so?

00:05:19.430 --> 00:05:24.230
I'm not tall at all. I'd like to know your secret.

00:05:24.230 --> 00:05:26.430
But being tall isn't always a good thing.

00:05:26.430 --> 00:05:28.800
I outgrow my clothes way too fast.

00:05:28.800 --> 00:05:30.810
Ehh? Is that so?

00:05:30.810 --> 00:05:35.340
The clothes I bought last year are too small this year.

00:05:35.340 --> 00:05:37.480
I kinda like them too, so it's kinda upsetting...

00:05:37.480 --> 00:05:39.610
So you have those kinds of problems...

00:05:39.610 --> 00:05:40.650
Yeah.

00:05:40.650 --> 00:05:43.320
I'm going to have a birthday party at my house soon,

00:05:43.320 --> 00:05:44.720
but I don't have anything to wear.

00:05:44.720 --> 00:05:45.990
Nothing to wear?

00:05:45.990 --> 00:05:50.490
Hadzuki-chan has a lot of clothes, so you can borrow some from her.

00:05:52.660 --> 00:05:56.410
I think this one fits Okuyama-san.

00:06:00.340 --> 00:06:02.090
I told ya, she ain't an actress.

00:06:02.090 --> 00:06:06.800
B-Besides, Hadzuki-chan's size is too small for me.

00:06:06.800 --> 00:06:09.240
Skirts, don't you have any skirts?

00:06:09.240 --> 00:06:11.680
Ah, y-yeah, skirts.

00:06:11.680 --> 00:06:12.510
Well...

00:06:15.050 --> 00:06:16.230
How about this one?

00:06:16.230 --> 00:06:20.190
Hadzuki-chan, do you wear that one, too?

00:06:20.190 --> 00:06:23.390
No, I've never worn it before.

00:06:23.390 --> 00:06:26.130
I can never guess what'll come outta her closet next.

00:06:26.130 --> 00:06:27.260
What do you think of it?

00:06:27.260 --> 00:06:30.620
Well... It's so luxurious.

00:06:30.620 --> 00:06:32.660
Just say ya hate it!

00:06:32.660 --> 00:06:34.370
Y-Yeah...

00:06:34.370 --> 00:06:37.330
Okuyama-san, what kind of clothes do you like?

00:06:37.330 --> 00:06:45.550
Well... Actually, I had a dress when I was small. I wish I could wear it again.

00:06:45.550 --> 00:06:47.180
When you were small?

00:06:47.180 --> 00:06:51.050
I grew very fast, so I've only worn it once.

00:06:51.050 --> 00:06:54.430
Ehh? What did it look like? Draw a picture for us.

00:06:55.360 --> 00:06:56.640
I'm a little surprised.

00:06:56.640 --> 00:07:02.030
Yeah I thought it'd be more sporty, the kinds where ya can move fast.

00:07:02.030 --> 00:07:05.630
I'm quite fond of these kinds of clothes, too.

00:07:05.630 --> 00:07:07.070
Really?

00:07:07.070 --> 00:07:10.400
Hadzuki-chan, I remember you have a similar dress, don't you?

00:07:11.710 --> 00:07:15.660
Let's go find it. Okuyama-san, please wait here.

00:07:15.660 --> 00:07:16.830
Right, right.

00:07:18.080 --> 00:07:22.930
Let's make a dress based on Okuyama-san's drawing with our magic.

00:07:22.930 --> 00:07:24.970
Ah! I get it now.

00:07:24.970 --> 00:07:30.090
We're gonna make any clothes Okuyama-san wants with magic.

00:07:30.090 --> 00:07:31.180
Now then.

00:07:31.760 --> 00:07:34.180
Just leave the spell to me.

00:07:48.010 --> 00:07:50.950
Pretty Witchy Hadzuki-chi!

00:07:51.980 --> 00:07:56.410
Paipai Ponpoi Puwapuwa Puu!

00:07:56.410 --> 00:07:59.790
Make a dress like the drawing!

00:08:02.860 --> 00:08:04.190
Happy birthday!

00:08:04.190 --> 00:08:05.540
Happy birthday, Okuyama-san.

00:08:05.540 --> 00:08:08.030
It's so cute. That dress is so cute!

00:08:08.030 --> 00:08:09.590
Thank you very much.

00:08:09.590 --> 00:08:11.730
You're cute wearing a dress.

00:08:11.730 --> 00:08:15.700
Ya look different wearin' a dress.

00:08:16.370 --> 00:08:19.180
Well, it doesn't really suit me, does it?

00:08:19.180 --> 00:08:21.890
Come on, you look great!

00:08:21.890 --> 00:08:24.680
Y-You think so?

00:08:24.680 --> 00:08:27.820
Thanks, but it's a little embarrassing.

00:08:27.820 --> 00:08:29.380
It really suits ya.

00:08:29.380 --> 00:08:31.890
Hey, Hadzuki-chan, don'tcha think so too?

00:08:31.890 --> 00:08:33.820
Hm? Yeah...

00:08:33.820 --> 00:08:36.160
What's the matter, Hadzuki-chan?

00:08:36.160 --> 00:08:38.330
Yeah! Go get her present.

00:08:44.370 --> 00:08:47.870
Didn't I tell ya she ain't an actress?

00:08:47.870 --> 00:08:49.170
Well, it doesn't matter.

00:08:51.260 --> 00:08:55.580
Happy birthday, Okuyama-san.

00:08:55.580 --> 00:08:56.470
Thanks.

00:08:56.470 --> 00:08:59.980
I'm so glad you brought a bouquet of flowers.

00:08:59.980 --> 00:09:02.180
I feel like a star.

00:09:03.650 --> 00:09:04.920
Bye-bye.

00:09:04.920 --> 00:09:06.750
Thanks for everything today.

00:09:06.750 --> 00:09:08.090
See you tomorrow.

00:09:08.090 --> 00:09:11.150
Please come on my next birthday.

00:09:11.150 --> 00:09:13.460
Sure, I'll be there!

00:09:13.460 --> 00:09:15.940
Okuyama-san, ya don't hafta see us off.

00:09:15.940 --> 00:09:19.070
Ehhh? I want to walk with you a bit more.

00:09:19.070 --> 00:09:22.620
We can go home by ourselves from here.

00:09:22.620 --> 00:09:24.080
R-Really?

00:09:25.960 --> 00:09:27.610
SOS.

00:09:27.610 --> 00:09:28.630
What?

00:09:30.400 --> 00:09:32.210
You look different.

00:09:32.210 --> 00:09:34.410
What's wrong with that?

00:09:34.410 --> 00:09:38.590
Yeah, sometimes I just want to change my image.

00:09:38.590 --> 00:09:42.620
Hmph! That dress doesn't suit you!

00:09:42.620 --> 00:09:43.470
It's disgusting.

00:09:43.470 --> 00:09:45.360
You're so rude!

00:09:45.360 --> 00:09:47.760
Yeah! Take that back!

00:09:47.760 --> 00:09:50.900
If ya don't, I ain't gonna be so nice with ya!

00:09:50.900 --> 00:09:53.660
W-W-W-What's gotten into you all of a sudden?

00:09:53.660 --> 00:09:54.610
What's wrong with you?

00:09:57.570 --> 00:09:58.820
Okuyama-san?

00:10:00.830 --> 00:10:02.700
What's the matter?

00:10:10.890 --> 00:10:15.090
W-What? I only said it doesn't suit her? What's wrong with that?

00:10:17.890 --> 00:10:20.260
Sagawa! Ya made her cry!

00:10:20.260 --> 00:10:23.140
W-What do you mean? Was it something I did?

00:10:23.140 --> 00:10:25.200
Of course it was!

00:10:25.200 --> 00:10:27.740
Forget it, Doremi-chan.

00:10:29.980 --> 00:10:31.470
Okuyama-san!

00:10:34.280 --> 00:10:35.650
This is all your fault Sagawa!

00:10:35.650 --> 00:10:37.780
M-My fault?

00:10:37.780 --> 00:10:40.880
Okuyama-san is hurt because of you!

00:10:40.880 --> 00:10:42.350
The three of us...

00:10:42.350 --> 00:10:43.950
will never forgive you!

00:10:43.950 --> 00:10:46.120
This is bad! Run!

00:10:46.120 --> 00:10:49.500
Stop! Don't you run away!

00:10:53.420 --> 00:10:55.530
Jeez...

00:10:55.530 --> 00:10:57.760
What's there to cry about?

00:10:58.800 --> 00:11:03.010
Don't worry, she'll forget it by tomorrow.

00:11:04.310 --> 00:11:05.970
You think?

00:11:31.000 --> 00:11:32.330
She's late.

00:11:32.330 --> 00:11:34.670
I don't want to get beat up so early in the morning.

00:11:34.670 --> 00:11:38.550
Yeah, she's probably still angry.

00:11:40.510 --> 00:11:41.840
Ah! Here she comes!

00:11:47.980 --> 00:11:49.390
She's the same as usual.

00:11:49.390 --> 00:11:51.550
Good morning, Okuyama-san.

00:11:51.550 --> 00:11:52.490
Good morning.

00:11:52.490 --> 00:11:53.400
Good morning!

00:11:54.560 --> 00:11:57.330
Thank you for giving me such a great present yesterday.

00:11:57.330 --> 00:11:59.260
Yer welcome. Invite us again next time!

00:11:59.260 --> 00:11:59.780
Sure.

00:11:59.780 --> 00:12:00.820
Alright.

00:12:00.820 --> 00:12:02.600
Ta-da!

00:12:02.600 --> 00:12:05.100
Here comes the SOS!

00:12:05.100 --> 00:12:08.570
Good morning. Now we're talking nonsense, pon pon pon pon!

00:12:08.570 --> 00:12:11.710
Ponpoko is the sound of the racoon's stomach.

00:12:11.710 --> 00:12:16.900
And that was the SOS Trio! Give us a smile...

00:12:17.840 --> 00:12:20.050
That didn't work.

00:12:21.220 --> 00:12:24.900
What did we do wrong? I don't understand.

00:12:24.900 --> 00:12:28.890
What should we do? Come on! Come on! Tell us!

00:12:29.600 --> 00:12:31.100
You're the worst!

00:12:32.390 --> 00:12:34.800
Can't ya do any better?

00:12:34.800 --> 00:12:35.660
You're too cold.

00:12:35.660 --> 00:12:39.730
Rather than telling lame jokes, why don't you just apologize to Okuyama-san?

00:12:40.730 --> 00:12:42.370
That's right.

00:12:42.370 --> 00:12:45.860
Yeah, it's no use beating around the bush.

00:12:45.860 --> 00:12:50.280
It might not be working today, but we'll think of something tomorrow.

00:12:50.280 --> 00:12:53.580
But... It's not a bad idea to apologize directly.

00:12:55.290 --> 00:12:57.000
What is it? What is it?

00:12:58.020 --> 00:13:00.380
I don't really get it... But, I'm sorry.

00:13:01.460 --> 00:13:04.470
Sagawa is quite a gentleman.

00:13:04.470 --> 00:13:10.030
Actually, I don't know why you were crying at all.

00:13:10.030 --> 00:13:14.100
But if you're upset because of what I said, I apologize.

00:13:14.100 --> 00:13:14.940
I'm sorry.

00:13:14.940 --> 00:13:19.650
It's no use saying that now! What you said really hurt.

00:13:20.860 --> 00:13:22.240
But...

00:13:22.240 --> 00:13:23.310
But?

00:13:23.310 --> 00:13:26.250
If you can make me laugh from the bottom of my heart,

00:13:26.250 --> 00:13:27.780
I'll forgive you.

00:13:27.780 --> 00:13:28.920
Really?

00:13:28.920 --> 00:13:31.900
From the bottom of my heart. From the bottom of my heart.

00:13:31.900 --> 00:13:33.410
Alright.

00:13:35.830 --> 00:13:38.730
What's goin' on now? Things are gettin' complicated.

00:13:38.730 --> 00:13:41.860
I can't think of anyone who has laughed at the SOS Trio.

00:13:41.860 --> 00:13:43.760
Yeah, I can't either.

00:13:43.760 --> 00:13:45.720
Okuyama, we're going to start.

00:13:45.720 --> 00:13:46.680
Okay.

00:13:46.680 --> 00:13:50.570
You're gonna laugh! No! No! Circle around.

00:13:50.570 --> 00:13:54.700
Our gag will make you laugh, gang leader.

00:13:54.700 --> 00:13:59.040
You're gonna laugh and have fun until you die and go to Heaven.

00:14:01.320 --> 00:14:02.360
Good-bye.

00:14:02.360 --> 00:14:04.030
G-Good-bye?

00:14:04.030 --> 00:14:07.280
You can't go! You can't! A small turtle walks really slow!

00:14:07.280 --> 00:14:09.060
How cold...

00:14:09.060 --> 00:14:11.780
Ah! Sagawa-kun looks really upset by this.

00:14:13.700 --> 00:14:16.130
I haven't seen Sagawa like this before.

00:14:16.130 --> 00:14:19.120
She said good-bye to him. It's really hard to accept.

00:14:19.120 --> 00:14:20.340
But honestly...

00:14:20.340 --> 00:14:25.570
I'm afraid it's impossible for the SOS to make Okuyama-san laugh from the bottom of her heart.

00:14:25.570 --> 00:14:26.260
Don't you think so?

00:14:26.260 --> 00:14:27.050
Agreed.

00:14:27.050 --> 00:14:28.090
Yeah.

00:14:30.750 --> 00:14:35.220
So that's how it is. Girls have very complicated minds.

00:14:35.220 --> 00:14:37.990
Those guys have no talent in comedy.

00:14:37.990 --> 00:14:40.940
Doremi doesn't have any talent in magic, either.

00:14:43.480 --> 00:14:44.850
I'm sorry you think that.

00:14:48.630 --> 00:14:49.660
That's it!

00:14:50.160 --> 00:14:51.370
We could use magic!

00:14:51.370 --> 00:14:53.170
Ai-chan, Hadzuki-chan.

00:14:53.170 --> 00:14:53.910
Let's do it!

00:14:53.910 --> 00:14:54.590
Yeah!

00:15:08.620 --> 00:15:10.720
Pretty Witchy Doremi-chi!

00:15:32.070 --> 00:15:35.030
Pretty Witchy Hadzuki-chi!

00:15:56.930 --> 00:15:59.180
Pretty Witchy Aiko-chi!

00:16:10.880 --> 00:16:14.070
Please understand my feelings!

00:16:14.070 --> 00:16:17.590
Please forgive us! Fire, fire, firefly!

00:16:17.590 --> 00:16:20.790
We're so so so sorry!

00:16:20.790 --> 00:16:23.260
This is hopeless.

00:16:23.260 --> 00:16:24.860
It ain't workin'.

00:16:25.930 --> 00:16:29.340
Hadzuki-chan, were you laughing just now?

00:16:29.340 --> 00:16:30.160
Was I?

00:16:30.160 --> 00:16:33.070
Yeah! How could anyone laugh at such a cold joke?

00:16:33.070 --> 00:16:34.500
Y-Yeah.

00:16:34.500 --> 00:16:36.070
So, what are we gonna do?

00:16:36.070 --> 00:16:40.140
Aren't we going to make the SOS's jokes funny with magic?

00:16:40.140 --> 00:16:42.880
Ain't that too difficult for us?

00:16:42.880 --> 00:16:45.190
But we have Magical Stage.

00:16:45.190 --> 00:16:46.740
Will that work?

00:16:46.740 --> 00:16:50.910
Even with Magical Stage, if it can't be done, it can't be done.

00:16:50.910 --> 00:16:55.610
It will work if the three of us work together, right?

00:16:55.610 --> 00:16:56.660
Ya think?

00:16:56.660 --> 00:16:59.160
Well, either way, let's give it a try.

00:17:02.580 --> 00:17:05.570
Pirika Pirilala Carefreely!

00:17:07.040 --> 00:17:10.430
Paipai Ponpoi Flexibly!

00:17:11.550 --> 00:17:14.540
Pameruku Laruku Proudly!

00:17:16.010 --> 00:17:18.340
Magical Stage!

00:17:24.940 --> 00:17:28.420
Make the SOS Trio's jokes funny!

00:17:33.830 --> 00:17:34.360
Did it work?

00:17:34.360 --> 00:17:34.990
Let's check it out.

00:17:36.000 --> 00:17:38.760
Please give me some chocolate.

00:17:38.760 --> 00:17:40.870
The deluxe steak is so luxurious.

00:17:40.870 --> 00:17:42.870
I want that. I want... Double crackers.

00:17:42.870 --> 00:17:46.040
It doesn't look like anything has changed.

00:17:49.810 --> 00:17:51.030
Frogs?

00:17:51.030 --> 00:17:52.630
Why are there frogs?

00:17:59.090 --> 00:18:01.790
What's going on? The frogs are surrounding us!

00:18:01.790 --> 00:18:04.090
In that case, let's go home! (Kaeru = "go home" and "frog")

00:18:04.090 --> 00:18:04.960
How about that?

00:18:04.960 --> 00:18:10.020
Cut the crap! I'm afraid of frogs!

00:18:18.070 --> 00:18:20.410
What's going on anyway?

00:18:20.410 --> 00:18:22.040
Let's follow Sagawa.

00:18:22.040 --> 00:18:23.200
A-Alright.

00:18:23.830 --> 00:18:25.700
We'll follow them, too.

00:18:33.340 --> 00:18:37.460
What's goin' on? What about the SOS's jokes?

00:18:37.460 --> 00:18:41.220
Perhaps this kind of magic is too difficult for us.

00:18:41.220 --> 00:18:44.460
What do we do? We didn't mean for this to happen.

00:18:44.460 --> 00:18:49.870
Somebody, help! I don't remember being liked by frogs!

00:18:52.610 --> 00:18:54.640
Okuyama, help me.

00:18:54.640 --> 00:18:55.810
What's wrong?

00:18:55.810 --> 00:18:59.880
I'm not sure. A bunch of frogs came after me all of a sudden.

00:19:06.290 --> 00:19:08.660
Okuyama, do something.

00:19:08.660 --> 00:19:10.900
I'm afraid of frogs, too!

00:19:10.900 --> 00:19:11.710
Don't say such a thing!

00:19:11.710 --> 00:19:14.040
What should I say then?

00:19:15.730 --> 00:19:17.340
A-Anyway...

00:19:17.340 --> 00:19:18.220
Run!

00:19:27.610 --> 00:19:29.910
No, I can't run anymore.

00:19:29.910 --> 00:19:31.080
I give up.

00:19:31.080 --> 00:19:33.650
No, I'm not giving up yet.

00:19:33.650 --> 00:19:37.650
What? You always talk big, but you're always the first one to give up.

00:19:45.730 --> 00:19:46.660
Darn it.

00:19:57.570 --> 00:19:58.590
Hurry!

00:20:06.350 --> 00:20:08.480
What's going on?

00:20:08.480 --> 00:20:09.520
It's so weird.

00:20:09.520 --> 00:20:11.590
But it looks okay to me.

00:20:17.490 --> 00:20:18.440
Okuyama.

00:20:18.440 --> 00:20:22.530
What's with that? You look like an idiot!

00:20:22.530 --> 00:20:26.900
You're strange yourself. Go look in a mirror!

00:20:26.900 --> 00:20:29.240
I'm not as strange as you.

00:20:34.210 --> 00:20:35.380
She laughed.

00:20:37.380 --> 00:20:39.410
Okuyama is laughing.

00:20:39.410 --> 00:20:42.090
Although I don't know what's going on, but that's good.

00:20:42.090 --> 00:20:45.020
Do you remember our agreement?

00:20:45.020 --> 00:20:46.620
I do! I do!

00:20:46.620 --> 00:20:47.760
You laughed.

00:20:47.760 --> 00:20:50.770
Yes, I-I'm laughing! I'm laughing!

00:20:50.770 --> 00:20:52.980
Is it from the bottom of your heart?

00:20:52.980 --> 00:20:55.320
I said I'm laughing, right?

00:20:58.480 --> 00:21:02.580
That's fine and all, but how long are you going to keep laughing?

00:21:02.580 --> 00:21:07.160
Does it matter if I keep laughing? It's really hilarious.

00:21:07.160 --> 00:21:11.080
I really don't understand the magic this time.

00:21:11.080 --> 00:21:14.270
Okuyama-san is laughing, so it's all good.

00:21:14.270 --> 00:21:15.580
Hey...

00:21:15.580 --> 00:21:21.050
Is the magic to make the SOS's jokes funnier really that difficult for us?

00:21:21.050 --> 00:21:22.750
We did good, didn't we?

00:21:22.750 --> 00:21:25.820
But I don't think we did that.

00:21:27.160 --> 00:21:28.350
Good morning!

00:21:29.040 --> 00:21:30.380
Good morning!

00:21:30.380 --> 00:21:32.680
Yay! Women!

00:21:32.680 --> 00:21:34.180
What did you say?

00:21:34.180 --> 00:21:35.770
Run!

00:21:35.770 --> 00:21:36.940
The gorilla is angry!

00:21:36.940 --> 00:21:39.670
Scatter about until you reach Antarctica!

00:21:39.670 --> 00:21:41.640
Stop!

00:21:44.710 --> 00:21:46.850
They're all the same.

00:21:46.850 --> 00:21:47.980
Yeah.

00:21:47.980 --> 00:21:50.210
I wish they'd cut it out.

00:22:01.920 --> 00:22:03.600
Majo Rika was sold to Pop?

00:22:03.600 --> 00:22:05.870
Doremi-chan, yer the one who said she was fer sale!

00:22:05.870 --> 00:22:08.570
I didn't know Pop would actually buy her!

00:22:08.570 --> 00:22:10.970
We'll have to think of something to help Majo Rika!

00:22:10.970 --> 00:22:15.510
How are we going to help her out when the kids are fighting over her?

00:22:15.510 --> 00:22:16.740
That'll be a problem...

00:22:16.740 --> 00:22:19.310
But why is Majo Rika so popular?

00:22:19.310 --> 00:22:21.680
Kindergarteners these days.

00:22:22.380 --> 00:22:23.620
Ojamajo Doremi!

00:22:23.620 --> 00:22:25.710
Majo Rika Goes to Kindergarten.

00:22:25.890 --> 00:22:29.010
Happy! Lucky! For all of you!
